From d9bc686a042a15de84d5971434f21ad7493ce045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mano Thanabalan <mano.thanabalan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:48:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] radio_planner: run the arbiter on the no-task IRQ path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A task enqueued while a stale radio_irq_flag was pending skipped its
inline arbiter (rp_task_enqueue runs the arbiter only when no flag is
pending). The no-task branch was the only pass that could launch it —
but it only cleared the flag and slept the radio. An enqueued ASAP task
was then never launched: ASAP tasks don't arm the planner timer and
rp_callback early-returns once both flags clear, so the chip slept
forever while the host believed the radio was armed (RX submit returned
OK, chip RX counters flat until an MCU reset).
---
 smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c b/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
index 4b8e8d9..48cd248 100644
--- a/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
+++ b/smtc_rac_lib/radio_planner/src/radio_planner.c
@@ -589,6 +589,18 @@ void rp_callback( radio_planner_t* rp )
                 }
             }
             SMTC_MODEM_HAL_TRACE_PRINTF( " radio planner it but no more task activated\n" );
+            // A task enqueued while a stale radio_irq_flag was pending
+            // skipped its inline arbiter (rp_task_enqueue runs the arbiter
+            // only when no flag is pending). This branch was the only pass
+            // that could launch it — but it only cleared the flag and slept
+            // the radio. An enqueued ASAP task was then never launched:
+            // ASAP tasks don't arm the planner timer and rp_callback
+            // early-returns once both flags clear, so the chip slept
+            // forever while the host believed the radio was armed (RX
+            // submit returned OK, chip RX counters flat). Run the arbiter
+            // so the enqueued task launches; the launch callbacks re-start
+            // the TCXO and wake the radio.
+            rp_task_arbiter( rp, __func__ );
         }
 
         smtc_modem_hal_set_ant_switch( false );
-- 
